   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "06c84253",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Missing Station Information\n",
    "\n",
    "A substantial proportion of rides contained missing station identifiers and station names, particularly for trip start and end locations.\n",
    "\n",
    "Further investigation revealed that missing station data was overwhelmingly associated with electric bikes:\n",
    "- 100% of rides with missing start station IDs were electric bikes\n",
    "- More than 99% of rides with missing end station IDs were electric bikes\n",
    "\n",
    "This strongly suggests that the missing values are not random data quality issues, but instead reflect operational characteristics of Cyclistic’s electric bike system. Electric bikes likely support more flexible ride initiation or ride termination workflows, including station-free parking or GPS-based trip tracking.\n",
    "\n",
    "Additionally, these rides were used by both members and casual riders, indicating that the behavior represents a legitimate and meaningful usage pattern rather than anomalous customer activity.\n",
    "\n",
    "Because the missing station values appear structurally linked to electric bike operations rather than corrupted records, these observations were retained and handled selectively depending on the analytical context. Station-based analyses used filtered subsets where station information was required, while broader behavioral analyses preserved the full dataset."
   ]
