 "source": [
  "## Data Cleaning & Quality Assurance Summary\n",
  "\n",
  "This section details the critical data cleaning and quality assurance processes applied to the raw Cyclistic trip data. The primary objective is to establish a robust and reliable dataset suitable for in-depth analytical exploration, ensuring an immutable source of truth for all subsequent insights.\n",
  "\n",
  "### Data Hygiene Standards\n",
  "\n",
  "Rigorous checks were performed to uphold data integrity and eliminate erroneous records:\n",
  "\n",
  "1.  **Duplicate `ride_id` Elimination**: Ensured uniqueness of each ride transaction. Initial assessment confirmed no duplicate `ride_id` entries were present in the dataset, affirming the integrity of the primary identifier.\n",
  "2.  **Invalid & Non-Meaningful `ride_length_min` Removal**: Anomalous `ride_length_min` values were identified and addressed:\n",
  "    *   **Negative Durations**: 29 rides exhibited negative durations, indicating timestamp inconsistencies (e.g., `ended_at` preceding `started_at`).\n",
  "    *   **Ultra-Short Rides (< 1 minute)**: 155,603 additional rides were recorded with durations less than one minute. Further analysis revealed these were almost exclusively electric bikes (99.99%) and predominantly casual riders (approximately 90%). These short durations are considered non-meaningful for behavioral analysis, likely representing failed unlocks, accidental starts, or brief exploratory sessions, rather than genuine usage.\n",
  "    All 155,632 rides with `ride_length_min < 1` (which includes the 29 negative durations) were removed from the dataset to ensure focus on meaningful rider activity.\n",
  "\n",
  "### Business Rules Enforced & Null Value Handling\n",
  "\n",
 ],
